{"code":"de","name":"German","native":"Deutsch","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A2","level":{"title":"Elementary: city, travel, routines, health","goals":["Find your way around a German city","Talk about past trips with Perfekt","Describe routines, health, and future plans"],"units":[{"id":"A2-U1","title":"Getting around","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U1-L1","title":"Around the city (Wo? vs Wohin?)","learn":"Two questions rule German places! WO? (where?) → IN DER Stadt (dative, staying). WOHIN? (where to?) → IN DIE Stadt (accusative, going). Ich bin IN DER Schule vs Ich gehe IN DIE Schule.","vocab":[{"t":"die Straße","r":"dee SHTRAH-suh","en":"street","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Platz","r":"dehr plahts","en":"square","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Bahnhof","r":"dehr BAHN-hohf","en":"station","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Bank","r":"dee bahnk","en":"bank","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Krankenhaus","r":"dahss KRAHN-ken-hows","en":"hospital","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Geschäft","r":"dahss guh-SHEFT","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"links","r":"links","en":"left","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"rechts","r":"rekhts","en":"right","pos":"adverb"}],"grammar":{"title":"WO? (in der) vs WOHIN? (in die)","explain":"Staying → dative: IN DER Schule, IM Park (in+dem=im). Going → accusative: IN DIE Schule, INS Kino (in+das=ins). Movement changes the article!","pattern":"wo? + in der/im · wohin? + in die/ins","examples":[{"t":"Ich bin in der Stadt.","r":"eekh been in dehr shtaht.","en":"I am in the city. (staying)"},{"t":"Ich gehe in die Stadt.","r":"eekh GEH-uh in dee shtaht.","en":"I go into the city. (moving)"},{"t":"Er ist im Park.","r":"ehr ist im pahrk.","en":"He is in the park."}],"mistakes":["Saying IN DIE Stadt for staying — staying is IN DER (dative).","Forgetting IM = in+dem and INS = in+das shortcuts."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Entschuldigung, wo ist der Bahnhof?","r":"ent-SHOOL-dee-goong, voh ist dehr BAHN-hohf?","en":"Excuse me, where is the station?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Er ist dort, rechts.","r":"ehr ist dohrt, rekhts.","en":"It is over there, on the right."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ist es weit?","r":"ist ess vyet?","en":"Is it far?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Nein, es ist nah. Fünf Minuten.","r":"neyen, ess ist nah. fewnf mee-NOO-ten.","en":"No, it is near. Five minutes."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Wo ist der Bahnhof?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ich bin in ___ Stadt. (staying)","answer":"der"},{"type":"choose","q":"'It is near' is…","options":["Es ist weit","Es ist nah","Er ist nah","Es bist nah"],"answer":"Es ist nah"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: der / bin / Stadt / in / ich","answer":"ich bin in der Stadt"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Wo ist die Bank?","answer":"Wo ist die Bank?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH BIN IN DER STADT means…","options":["I go into the city","I am in the city","my city is big","I like cities"],"answer":1,"why":"Bin + in der = staying."},{"q":"RECHTS is…","options":["left","right","straight","back"],"answer":1,"why":"Rechts = right."},{"q":"Going somewhere uses…","options":["dative (in der)","accusative (in die)","nominative","no article"],"answer":1,"why":"Movement = accusative."},{"q":"WO IST DER BAHNHOF? means…","options":["Who is at the station?","Where is the station?","How is the station?","What is a station?"],"answer":1,"why":"Wo + ist = where is."},{"q":"FÜNF MINUTEN is…","options":["five minutes","ten minutes","five hours","five days"],"answer":0,"why":"Fünf = 5."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"City worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["street","station","shop"],"key":["die Straße","der Bahnhof","das Geschäft"]},{"instruction":"Wo? or Wohin? (der/die).","items":["Ich bin in ___ Stadt (staying)","Ich gehe in ___ Stadt (going)","Er ist im ___ (park)"],"key":["der","die","Park"]},{"instruction":"Ask for directions.","items":["Where is the bank?","Is it far?"],"key":["Wo ist die Bank?","Ist es weit?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U1-L2","title":"Travel and Perfekt","learn":"Past trips use PERFEKT: HABEN + past verb. ICH HABE BESUCHT = I visited. TU… wait — ICH HABE, DU HAST, ER HAT + GE-verb: besucht, gemacht, gekauft. GE- opens most past verbs!","vocab":[{"t":"die Reise","r":"dee RY-zuh","en":"trip","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Flugzeug","r":"dahss FLOOK-tsoyk","en":"plane","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Hotel","r":"dahss hoh-TELL","en":"hotel","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Koffer","r":"dehr KOH-fer","en":"suitcase","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Fahrkarte","r":"dee FAHR-kahr-tuh","en":"ticket","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Strand","r":"dehr shtrahnt","en":"beach","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Berg","r":"dehr behrk","en":"mountain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Foto","r":"dahss FOH-toh","en":"photo","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Perfekt: ich habe besucht","explain":"ICH HABE + besucht = I visited. DU HAST + gemacht = you made. ER HAT + gekauft = he bought. The GE-verb jumps to the END of the sentence!","pattern":"ich habe/du hast/er hat + … + GE-verb (at end)","examples":[{"t":"Ich habe Spanien besucht.","r":"eekh HAH-buh SHPAN-yen buh-ZOOKHT.","en":"I visited Spain."},{"t":"Hast du Fahrkarten gekauft?","r":"hahst doo FAHR-kahr-ten guh-KOWFT?","en":"Did you buy tickets?"},{"t":"Sie ist gestern angekommen.","r":"zee ist GES-tern AHN-guh-koh-men.","en":"She arrived yesterday. (sein verb!)"}],"mistakes":["Putting the GE-verb early — it goes to the END.","Forgetting movement verbs use SEIN: SIE IST angekommen."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Bist du diesen Sommer gereist?","r":"bist doo DEE-zen ZOH-mer guh-REYEST?","en":"Did you travel this summer?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Ja, ich habe Mexiko besucht. Ich war am Strand.","r":"yah, eekh HAH-buh MEK-see-koh buh-ZOOKHT. eekh vahr ahm shtrahnt.","en":"Yes, I visited Mexico. I was at the beach."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Hat es dir gefallen?","r":"haht ess deer guh-FAH-len?","en":"Did you like it?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Es war super!","r":"ess vahr ZOO-per!","en":"It was great!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I visited Spain","answer":"Ich habe Spanien besucht"},{"type":"fill","q":"Hast du Fahrkarten ___? (bought)","answer":"gekauft"},{"type":"choose","q":"'She arrived yesterday' uses…","options":["hat angekommen","ist angekommen","ankommt","angekommen hat"],"answer":"ist angekommen"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: besucht / habe / Spanien / ich","answer":"ich habe Spanien besucht"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich habe Mexiko besucht.","answer":"Ich habe Mexiko besucht."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH HABE BESUCHT means…","options":["I visit","I visited","you visited","he visits"],"answer":1,"why":"Habe + GE-verb = past."},{"q":"DER KOFFER is…","options":["ticket","suitcase","hotel","beach"],"answer":1,"why":"Koffer = suitcase."},{"q":"HAT ES DIR GEFALLEN? means…","options":["Did you like it?","Do you like it?","Will you like it?","You like it!"],"answer":0,"why":"Past: did it please you."},{"q":"Which is 'you bought'?","options":["ich habe gekauft","du hast gekauft","er hat gekauft","kaufen"],"answer":1,"why":"Du hast + GE-verb."},{"q":"GESTERN means…","options":["tomorrow","today","yesterday","now"],"answer":2,"why":"Gestern = yesterday."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Travel worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["trip","ticket","beach"],"key":["die Reise","die Fahrkarte","der Strand"]},{"instruction":"Put BESUCHEN in Perfekt.","items":["I visited","you visited","she visited"],"key":["ich habe besucht","du hast besucht","sie hat besucht"]},{"instruction":"Answer about a trip.","items":["Did you travel? (yes)","Where? (Mexico)"],"key":["Ja, ich bin gereist","Ich habe Mexiko besucht"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U2","title":"Life and plans","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U2-L1","title":"Daily routines (separable verbs!)","learn":"German verbs SPLIT! AUFSTEHEN (to get up) → ICH STEHE AUF. The prefix jumps to the end: ANrufen → ICH RUFE AN. Morning verbs split daily: aufstehen, duschen (no split!), frühstücken, anfangen.","vocab":[{"t":"der Morgen","r":"dehr MOHR-gen","en":"morning","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Nachmittag","r":"dehr NAHKH-mit-tahk","en":"afternoon","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Abend","r":"dehr AH-bent","en":"evening","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Arbeit","r":"dee AHR-beyet","en":"work / job","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Schule","r":"dee SHOO-luh","en":"school","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Dusche","r":"dee DOO-shuh","en":"shower","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Frühstück","r":"dahss FREW-shtook","en":"breakfast","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Abendessen","r":"dahss AH-bent-es-sen","en":"dinner","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Separable verbs: ich stehe AUF","explain":"AUFSTEHEN splits: ICH STEHE AUF (I get up), DU STEHST AUF, ER STEHT AUF. Prefix (auf/an/mit/zu) jumps to the END. ANrufen → ICH RUFE dich AN (I call you).","pattern":"verb stem + ending … prefix (at end)","examples":[{"t":"Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf.","r":"eekh SHTEH-uh oom ZEE-ben oor owf.","en":"I get up at seven."},{"t":"Duschst du morgens?","r":"dooshst doo MOHR-gens?","en":"Do you shower in the mornings?"},{"t":"Er fängt spät an.","r":"ehr fengkt shpayt ahn.","en":"He starts late. (anfangen)"}],"mistakes":["Saying ICH AUFSTEHE — split it: ICH STEHE AUF!","Forgetting the prefix at the end — it must jump."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Wann stehst du auf?","r":"vahn shtayst doo owf?","en":"When do you get up?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf und dusche.","r":"eekh SHTEH-uh oom ZEE-ben oor owf oont DOO-shuh.","en":"I get up at seven and shower."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Frühstückst du?","r":"FREW-shtookst doo?","en":"Do you eat breakfast?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Ja, mit meiner Familie.","r":"yah, mit MEY-ner fah-MEE-lee-uh.","en":"Yes, with my family."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I get up at seven","answer":"Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ du morgens? (shower)","answer":"Duschst"},{"type":"choose","q":"'He starts late' is…","options":["Er fängt spät","Er fängt spät an","Er anfangt spät","Er anfängt"],"answer":"Er fängt spät an"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: auf / um / stehe / sieben / ich / Uhr","answer":"ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf.","answer":"Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH STEHE AUF means…","options":["I stand up (rise)","I get up (mornings)","I sit down","I run"],"answer":1,"why":"Aufstehen = to get up."},{"q":"DAS ABENDESSEN is…","options":["breakfast","lunch","dinner","snack"],"answer":2,"why":"Abendessen = dinner."},{"q":"WANN STEHST DU AUF? asks about…","options":["price","time","place","reason"],"answer":1,"why":"Wann = when."},{"q":"In AUFSTEHEN the prefix goes…","options":["nowhere","to the end","to the start","it vanishes"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich stehe AUF — jumps!."},{"q":"Which verb splits?","options":["lernen","aufstehen","sprechen","wohnen"],"answer":1,"why":"Aufstehen = auf + stehen. ."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Routines worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["morning","school","dinner"],"key":["der Morgen","die Schule","das Abendessen"]},{"instruction":"Split the verb.","items":["I get up at … (aufstehen)","You get up? (aufstehen)","He starts late (anfangen)"],"key":["Ich stehe um … Uhr auf","Stehst du auf?","Er fängt spät an"]},{"instruction":"Describe your morning.","items":["I get up at seven","I shower"],"key":["Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf","Ich dusche"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U2-L2","title":"Health and future (werden)","learn":"At the doctor: MEIN KOPF TUT WEH = my head hurts. Future with WERDEN: ICH WERDE REISEN = I will travel. ICH WERDE, DU WIRST, ER WIRD + verb-at-end. The plan verb jumps last!","vocab":[{"t":"der Kopf","r":"dehr kohpf","en":"head","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Hand","r":"dee hahnt","en":"hand","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Auge","r":"dahss OW-guh","en":"eye","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Arzt","r":"dehr ahrtst","en":"doctor","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Apotheke","r":"dee ah-poh-TEH-kuh","en":"pharmacy","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Schmerz","r":"dehr shmehrts","en":"pain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Fieber","r":"dahss FEE-ber","en":"fever","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Gesundheit","r":"dee guh-ZOONT-heyet","en":"health","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Future: ich werde … reisen (verb at end!)","explain":"ICH WERDE = I will, DU WIRST, ER WIRD. The main verb goes to the END: ICH WERDE MORGEN REISEN (I will travel tomorrow). Bookends: werde … reisen!","pattern":"ich werde/du wirst/er wird + … + verb (end)","examples":[{"t":"Ich werde reisen.","r":"eekh VEHR-duh REY-zen.","en":"I will travel."},{"t":"Wirst du lernen?","r":"veerst doo LEHR-nen?","en":"Will you learn?"},{"t":"Es wird regnen.","r":"ess veert REHK-nen.","en":"It is going to rain."}],"mistakes":["Putting the verb early: ICH WERDE REISEN (end!) — never ICH REISE WERDE.","Saying DU WERDE — you is DU WIRST."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Herr Doktor, mein Kopf tut weh.","r":"hehr DOHK-tohr, meyen kohpf toot veh.","en":"Doctor, my head hurts."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Hast du Fieber?","r":"hahst doo FEE-ber?","en":"Do you have a fever?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Nein, aber ich werde mich ausruhen.","r":"neyen, AH-ber eekh VEHR-duh meekh OWS-roo-en.","en":"No, but I will rest."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Gut. Du wirst gesund.","r":"goot. doo veerst guh-ZOONT.","en":"Good. You will get well."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I will travel","answer":"Ich werde reisen"},{"type":"fill","q":"Mein ___ tut weh. (head)","answer":"Kopf"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Will you learn?' is…","options":["Wirst du lernen?","Werde ich lernen?","Wird er lernen?","Werden wir lernen?"],"answer":"Wirst du lernen?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: reisen / werde / ich","answer":"ich werde reisen"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Mein Kopf tut weh.","answer":"Mein Kopf tut weh."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ICH WERDE REISEN means…","options":["I travel now","I travelled","I will travel","I want travel"],"answer":2,"why":"Werde + verb = future."},{"q":"MEIN KOPF TUT WEH means…","options":["my head hurts","my hand hurts","my eye hurts","my leg hurts"],"answer":0,"why":"Kopf = head."},{"q":"DIE APOTHEKE is…","options":["hospital","pharmacy","clinic","shop"],"answer":1,"why":"Apotheke = pharmacy."},{"q":"DU WIRST GESUND means…","options":["you were healthy","you will get well","you feel bad","you look fine"],"answer":1,"why":"Wirst + gesund."},{"q":"In the future, the main verb goes…","options":["first","to the end","nowhere","twice"],"answer":1,"why":"Ich werde … REISEN."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Health worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["head","doctor","fever"],"key":["der Kopf","der Arzt","das Fieber"]},{"instruction":"Write the plan.","items":["I will rest","You will get well"],"key":["Ich werde mich ausruhen","Du wirst gesund"]},{"instruction":"At the doctor.","items":["My head hurts","I have a fever"],"key":["Mein Kopf tut weh","Ich habe Fieber"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U3","title":"Shopping and weather","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U3-L1","title":"Clothes and shopping (dieser)","learn":"Shop in German! DAS HEMD, DIE SCHUHE. Point with DIESER (this, masculine), DIESE (feminine), DIESES (neuter): DIESES HEMD (this shirt), DIESER LADEN (this shop).","vocab":[{"t":"das Hemd","r":"dahss hempt","en":"shirt","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Hose","r":"dee HOH-zuh","en":"trousers","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Schuhe","r":"dee SHOO-uh","en":"shoes","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Kleid","r":"dahss klyet","en":"dress","pos":"noun"},{"t":"das Geschäft","r":"dahss guh-SHEFT","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Preis","r":"dehr pryess","en":"price","pos":"noun"},{"t":"billig","r":"BIL-likh","en":"cheap","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"teuer","r":"TOY-er","en":"expensive","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"DIESER/DIESE/DIESES: this","explain":"DIESER + masculine (dieser Hut), DIESE + feminine (diese Hose), DIESES + neuter (dieses Hemd). Plural: DIESE Schuhe. Same endings as DER/DIE/DAS — familiar music!","pattern":"dieser/diese/dieses + thing","examples":[{"t":"Dieses Hemd ist billig.","r":"DEE-zess hempt ist BIL-likh.","en":"This shirt is cheap."},{"t":"Dieser Laden ist teuer.","r":"DEE-zer LAH-den ist TOY-er.","en":"This shop is expensive."},{"t":"Diese Schuhe sind schön.","r":"DEE-zuh SHOO-uh zint shurn.","en":"These shoes are pretty."}],"mistakes":["Saying DIESER Hose — Hose is feminine: DIESE Hose.","Saying DIESES Hut — Hut is masculine: DIESER Hut."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Max","t":"Wie viel kostet dieses Hemd?","r":"vee feel KOHS-tet DEE-zess hempt?","en":"How much is this shirt?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Zwanzig Euro. Es ist billig.","r":"TSVAHN-tsikh oy-ROH. ess ist BIL-likh.","en":"Twenty euros. It is cheap."},{"sp":"Max","t":"Und dieses Kleid?","r":"oont DEE-zess klyet?","en":"And this dress?"},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Fünfzig Euro.","r":"FEWNF-tsikh oy-ROH.","en":"Fifty euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: This shirt is cheap","answer":"Dieses Hemd ist billig"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ Laden ist teuer. (this)","answer":"Dieser"},{"type":"choose","q":"'These shoes are pretty' is…","options":["Dieser Schuhe sind schön","Diese Schuhe sind schön","Dieses Schuhe ist schön","Die Schuhe sind schöne"],"answer":"Diese Schuhe sind schön"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: Hemd / billig / ist / dieses","answer":"dieses Hemd ist billig"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Wie viel kostet dieses Hemd?","answer":"Wie viel kostet dieses Hemd?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"DIESES HEMD means…","options":["that shirt","this shirt","those shirts","my shirt"],"answer":1,"why":"Dieses = this (neuter)."},{"q":"DIE HOSE is…","options":["shoes","trousers","shirt","dress"],"answer":1,"why":"Hose = trousers."},{"q":"WIE VIEL KOSTET…? asks about…","options":["size","price","colour","place"],"answer":1,"why":"Kostet = costs."},{"q":"DIESER is used with…","options":["feminine nouns","masculine nouns","plurals","verbs"],"answer":1,"why":"Dieser Hut — masculine."},{"q":"BILLIG means…","options":["expensive","cheap","big","new"],"answer":1,"why":"Billig = cheap."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Shopping worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["shirt","shoes","cheap"],"key":["das Hemd","die Schuhe","billig"]},{"instruction":"Choose dieser, diese, or dieses.","items":["___ Hemd (this)","___ Laden (this)","___ Schuhe (these)"],"key":["dieses","dieser","diese"]},{"instruction":"Ask prices.","items":["How much is this shirt?","How much is this dress?"],"key":["Wie viel kostet dieses Hemd?","Wie viel kostet dieses Kleid?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U3-L2","title":"Weather stories (war)","learn":"Weather stories use WAR (was): ES WAR SONNIG (it was sunny). ES GAB WIND (there was wind). ICH WAR, DU WARST, ER WAR — the simple past of SEIN, storytellers' favourite!","vocab":[{"t":"die Sonne","r":"dee ZON-nuh","en":"sun","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Regen","r":"dehr REH-gen","en":"rain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Kälte","r":"dee KEHL-tuh","en":"cold","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Hitze","r":"dee HIT-suh","en":"heat","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Sommer","r":"dehr ZOH-mer","en":"summer","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Winter","r":"dehr VIN-ter","en":"winter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"die Wolke","r":"dee VOHL-kuh","en":"cloud","pos":"noun"},{"t":"der Wind","r":"dehr vint","en":"wind","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"WAR: it was (simple past of SEIN)","explain":"ICH WAR = I was, DU WARST, ER WAR. ES WAR SONNIG = it was sunny. ES GAB + noun = there was…: ES GAB REGEN (there was rain).","pattern":"ich war/du warst/er war · es gab + thing","examples":[{"t":"Es war sonnig.","r":"ess vahr ZON-nikh.","en":"It was sunny."},{"t":"Es gab viel Wind.","r":"ess gahp feel vint.","en":"There was much wind."},{"t":"Gestern war es kalt.","r":"GES-tern vahr ess kahlt.","en":"Yesterday it was cold."}],"mistakes":["Saying ES HAT SONNIG for stories — weather past is ES WAR.","Saying ES GIBT for past — past needs ES GAB."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Lena","t":"Wie war das Wetter gestern?","r":"vee vahr dahss VET-ter GES-tern?","en":"How was the weather yesterday?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Es war sonnig. Es gab viel Sonne.","r":"ess vahr ZON-nikh. ess gahp feel ZON-nuh.","en":"It was sunny. There was much sun."},{"sp":"Lena","t":"Und heute?","r":"oont HOY-tuh?","en":"And today?"},{"sp":"Max","t":"Es regnet!","r":"ess REHK-net!","en":"It rains!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It was sunny","answer":"Es war sonnig"},{"type":"fill","q":"Es gab viel ___ (wind)","answer":"Wind"},{"type":"choose","q":"'There was sun' is…","options":["Es gibt Sonne","Es gab Sonne","Es war Sonne","Es ist Sonne"],"answer":"Es gab Sonne"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: sonnig / war / es","answer":"es war sonnig"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Es war sonnig.","answer":"Es war sonnig."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ES WAR SONNIG means…","options":["it is sunny","it was sunny","it will rain","it snowed"],"answer":1,"why":"War = was."},{"q":"DER REGEN is…","options":["sun","rain","wind","cloud"],"answer":1,"why":"Regen = rain."},{"q":"ES GAB VIEL WIND means…","options":["it is windy","there was much wind","wind comes","no wind"],"answer":1,"why":"Gab = there was."},{"q":"Weather in the past uses…","options":["Perfekt","war/gab","future","present"],"answer":1,"why":"War = was; gab = there was."},{"q":"WIE WAR DAS WETTER? asks…","options":["what time was it?","how was the weather?","where was he?","who came?"],"answer":1,"why":"Wetter = weather."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Weather worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to German.","items":["sun","rain","winter"],"key":["die Sonne","der Regen","der Winter"]},{"instruction":"Paint past skies.","items":["It was sunny","There was much wind","Yesterday it was cold"],"key":["Es war sonnig","Es gab viel Wind","Gestern war es kalt"]},{"instruction":"Talk weather.","items":["How was the weather yesterday?","And today?"],"key":["Wie war das Wetter gestern?","Und heute?"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A2 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Wo ist der Bahnhof?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ich bin in ___ Stadt (staying)","answer":"der"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I get up at seven'","options":["Ich aufstehe um sieben Uhr","Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf","Ich stehe auf um sieben Uhr","Auf ich stehe sieben Uhr"],"answer":"Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I will learn","answer":"Ich werde lernen"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"Mein Kopf tut weh.","answer":"My head hurts."},{"type":"fill","q":"Es ist ___ (near)","answer":"nah"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: gefallen / dir / es / hat","answer":"hat es dir gefallen"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Wo ist die Bank?","answer":"Wo ist die Bank?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Es ___ sonnig. (was)","answer":"war"},{"type":"choose","q":"'This shirt is cheap'","options":["Dieser Hemd ist billig","Dieses Hemd ist billig","Diese Hemd ist billig","Dieses Hemd billig ist"],"answer":"Dieses Hemd ist billig"}]}}}